{"title":"1973 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(similar_to_solution_1,_but_full_proof)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (similar to solution 1, but full proof)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> lie in the interior of a regular tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82cb802aef179231600293427a9b39af036b05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PAQ &lt; 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the side length of the regular tetrahedron be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Link and extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to meet the plane containing triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; link <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7563031eab26ad18658cf2f6a8e4948861bb9013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and extend it to meet the same plane at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are inside triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/072b031c4ff67af3d7dcc1d2270ad56c899eccfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAQ = \\angle EAF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Now let’s look at the plane containing triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> with points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside the triangle. Link and extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides to meet the sides of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58af38e8286edcd5a57363d7c65661421eb0ec58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAF &lt; \\angle IAJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"127\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are interior of the tetrahedron, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be both at the vertices and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e088b2e35b6fd2238a980d3fa1073963ee582399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IJ &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/7099eeab6cc3d3f355737dd3716b8a64d59dd18f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle IAJ &lt; \\angle BAD = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"170\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7fba0d5b781cffd07ff692d3adcd0064b065a41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAQ &lt; 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Solution with graphs posted at\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.cut-the-knot.org/wiki-math/index.php?n=MathematicalOlympiads.USA1973Problem1\">http://www.cut-the-knot.org/wiki-math/index.php?n=MathematicalOlympiads.USA1973Problem1</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28similar_to_solution_1.2C_but_full_proof.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(similar_to_solution_1,_but_full_proof)\">Solution 2 (similar to solution 1, but full proof)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (similar to solution 1, but full proof)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the side length of the regular tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7563031eab26ad18658cf2f6a8e4948861bb9013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> to intersect the plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/387e075a47d8539dd31f97961dd851ed863f9acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15bda2f23a7e2a0c5be295240e1c6dbf6553458e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. We can observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8de18dcb9d74b9dd30fa7e3bde34364b05816e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAQ=\\angle P&#39;AQ&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/58235ee706438b477de873005a8a7dec97ebb377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;Q&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> to intersect the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15bda2f23a7e2a0c5be295240e1c6dbf6553458e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8b3ed35fad6a211ca033d7daa4ab7fe61a8ea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c31ec0dd75e1a494df6da20f81757611030832b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" />. We can observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/76284a0d2079ab1cb0b20eda899abab4c7cf2fb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P&#39;AQ&#39;&lt;\\angle P&#39;&#39;AQ&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" />. We assume that, WLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8b3ed35fad6a211ca033d7daa4ab7fe61a8ea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c31ec0dd75e1a494df6da20f81757611030832b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let the ratios <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f659022d546bf18d0e929ccd5fcc52cd1ce4eaa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BP&#39;&#39;}{BD}=\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b5dab58f66a5ed40421e38b4ae2bc5eb931b82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BQ&#39;&#39;}{BC}=\\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"40\" />. We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7321cc5404a3af4dc24be928135b0a9de4a4cdb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu,\\lambda\\in (0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />. It follows from Stewart's theorem that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207470e26e20157fc18e90663d213efc651b9b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP&#39;&#39;^2=AD^2\\mu+AB^2(1-\\mu)-\\mu(1-\\mu)BD^2=(\\mu^2-\\mu+1)s\\\\ AQ&#39;&#39;^2=AC^2\\lambda+AB^2(1-\\lambda)-\\lambda(1-\\lambda)BC^2=(\\lambda^2-\\lambda^2+1)s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Furthermore, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a6a99c6af7810e839bc17325cc25a6de681aa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;&#39;C^2=CD^2\\mu+CB^2(1-\\mu)-\\mu(1-\\mu)BD^2=(\\mu^2-\\mu+1)s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"491\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Using this, we can conclude that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1ccf9d47b36e77f973de64a4ef0915d34749dd12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;&#39;Q&#39;&#39;^2=P&#39;&#39;C^2\\lambda+(BD\\mu)^2(1-\\lambda)-\\lambda(1-\\lambda)BC^2\\\\ =(\\mu\\lambda-\\mu-\\lambda+2)s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>By cosine law, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce9ea0b794f56d44810978d126df524984606654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\angle P&#39;&#39;AQ&#39;&#39;=\\frac{P&#39;&#39;A^2+Q&#39;&#39;A^2-P&#39;&#39;Q&#39;&#39;^2}{2P&#39;&#39;A\\cdot Q&#39;&#39;A}\\\\ =\\frac{\\mu\\lambda-\\mu-\\lambda+2}{2\\sqrt{(\\mu^2-\\mu+1)(\\lambda^2-\\lambda+1)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"91\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/884bf05806f253b1bd26bf2731291ada14f163ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu,\\lambda\\in(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We first find a lower bound of the numerator. We write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c2270a34275256d5e09ca6e93d51f1efdec3a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu\\lambda-\\mu-\\lambda+2=(\\lambda-1)\\mu-\\lambda+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"276\" height=\"20\" /> as a linear function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> by letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> be constant. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a2521da0a81cc9a9422b8f20f1f64ade3b8083.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda\\in (0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />, the coefficient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd23f254329a8263026e7ead134d5c5fe564c487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> in this linear function is negative, meaning this expression is least when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> is least \"at\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa99e0a8fbe96cb08b02d8a2db5a8c614986b48d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu\\lambda-\\mu-\\lambda+2&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now we find an upper bound of the denominator. We complete the square in the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f0301969ba3e110cdd9f81171062a99b8c7601f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{(\\mu^2-\\mu+1)(\\lambda^2-\\lambda+1)}=2\\sqrt{((\\mu-\\frac{1}{2})^2+\\frac{3}{4})((\\lambda-\\frac{1}{2})^2+\\frac{3}{4})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"507\" height=\"45\" /> which is least when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> \"are\" both 1. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b462e4e95918465f4063659047be137c1dcc578b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{(\\mu^2-\\mu+1)(\\lambda^2-\\lambda+1)}&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"255\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ced942b54d1a82cb053f684ee38780b9a827ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\angle P&#39;&#39;AQ&#39;&#39;&lt;\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" />, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18c33e3c02eb9ee624c48f299be57021071b7dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P&#39;&#39;AQ&#39;&#39;&lt;60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d23b11ac9d8ed03a65355f8c73bffb4959ef58c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAQ=\\angle P&#39;AQ&#39;&lt;\\angle P&#39;&#39;AQ&#39;&#39;&lt;60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"292\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p><p>hurdler: Remark on solution 1: This proof is not rigorous, in the very last step. The last step needs more justification.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO\" title=\"1973 USAMO\">1973 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1973 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" tit